  {
   "id": 548654,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/80762f156f4abc45.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Anna-Barbara Moscicki, et al./ScienceDirect)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>This illustration shows the incidence of human papillomavirus (HPV) infection and precancerous growths and cancer in different age groups.</p>\n<p>What is a conclusion we can reach based on this illustration?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1078043,
     "content_html": "High rates of HPV infection lead to high rates of precancerous growths."
    },
    {
     "id": 1078044,
     "content_html": "High rates of HPV infection lead to high rates of cancer."
    },
    {
     "id": 1078045,
     "content_html": "HPV incidence is not related to cancer incidences."
    },
    {
     "id": 1078046,
     "content_html": "HPV incidence is not related to precancerous growth incidences."
    }
   ],
